family,handler_path
# Example override of the family table (v4.1 section 5.2, requirement 3).
#
# To enable it: copy this file to `lookups/app_acl_family_map_override.csv` in the
# installed app, then describe one family per line. The real file is NEVER shipped in
# the archive: an app upgrade therefore cannot overwrite it, since the archive does not
# contain it. The counterpart is that a file living in `lookups/` is overwritten by an
# upgrade if it IS shipped - so back this one up before upgrading.
#
# `family` is the name of the generic stanza as it appears in `metadata/local.meta` -
# `views`, `savedsearches`, `workflow_actions` - and NOT the URI of a handler. The
# stanza name follows the underlying configuration file, not the URI: the handler
# `data/ui/workflow-actions` writes `[workflow_actions]`, with an underscore.
#
# It is loaded AFTER `bin/app_acl_family_map.json` and overrides it: a family present
# in both takes the value from this file.
#
# `handler_path` must match the pattern ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._~-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9._~-]+)*$
# - a non-conforming line is discarded and traced in the diagnostic log, never used. No
# derivation heuristic is applied (v4.1 section 5.2, requirement 2): a family absent
# from the table produces `acl_status=rejected`,
# `acl_error=unresolved_family:<family>`.
#
# THREE FAMILIES ARE KNOWN TO BE UNREACHABLE and are deliberately absent from the
# shipped table (v4.1 section 5.3): `visualizations` answers `500 No capability
# specified for action='edit'`, `ntags` does not support ACL at all, and `props`
# through `data/props/extractions` answers `400 Cannot parse object name` - `props` is
# reachable through seven other handlers, of which the shipped one. Overriding a family
# towards one of those paths produces an HTTP error per event, never a silent write.
#
# The two lines below are commented out: this example file must override nothing as it
# stands.
#an-unknown-family,data/ui/something
#another-family,admin/something-else
